{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/184210-choice-become-a-vampire-or-a-geist","id":184210,"title":"Choice: become a Vampire or a Geist","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-29T17:06:59-07:00","id":184210,"title":"Choice: become a Vampire or a Geist","content":"I thought this was a fun enough idea from the old forums to repost.<br /> <br /> sikker said:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Being bitten isn't enough to become a vampire, you also have to recieve blood and a dot of willpower from the vampire to seal the deal. It is theoratically possible to be contacted by a Geist at that exact second and be offered to return to life as a Bound instead of a Vampire. But it is one or the other. Accepting the Bargain makes the Embrace fail, and refusing the Bargain simply leaves the Embrace to work as normal.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">It *would* be an interesting story, though, to have a vampire Embrace a childe, and have it seemingly work, bringing the person back to life and able to perform magical tricks... But somehow that childe is able to eat food, age and walk in daylight. How long until it is discovered that the childe is not a vampire at all? </span></span></span><i>That</i><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"> would be an interesting game.</span></span></span></i> </div> </div> </div>What I'm thinking though that it'd be pretty cool in a campaign to offer the player that choice.<br /> <br /> You get jumped by vampires, and just at that moment when you are floating between life and death that is needed before you receive that drop of Vitae, this figure comes to you and says, basically: &quot;Look, those guys up there are going to make you one of them. You'll be forced to prey on others like they do and you'll be forever cursed. Why not take on my offer instead? I can bring you back same as you were.&quot;<br /> <br /> A pretty good backstory for a Sin-Eater, too. Brought back by a force greater than your assailants to take revenge on them, expecting to get a new childe and receiving a vengeful spirit who can roast their asses. And you are now the great protector of the spirit world, who makes the undead creatures of darkness flee and send them back to the underworld that they were seeking to escape.<br /> <br /> The challenge of course is to make this encounter meaningful if the player picks the vampire side, too. What is this mysterious otherworldy being messing with the Embraces? Is he perhaps a vengeful embodiment of failed embraces, or something even stranger? Did he also make that offer to others in the past, and what motivated them to refuse? Or maybe there are others like him too - an entire congregate of spirits opposing the vampiric race. Or maybe he is something personal to the character, a gatekeeper between life and death who shall appear again when the vampire reaches the end of their unlife, perhaps even a judge of their otherworldy judgement or a guide to Golconda?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T23:58:25-07:00","id":191157,"title":"","content":"Excellent moral dilemmas. But what about this: Okay, so you have been drained dry, the Geist is talking to you and telling these things as it offers you the Bargain. Moral Crossroad Theater aside, what really sounds more appealing; coming back from the dead a slavering corpse that feeds on the life blood of the living and gets the worst case of sunburn when the sun hasn't even risen over the horizon in exchange for possibly immortality and nifty powers.. OR coming back from the dead with a ghostly pseudo buddy, the ability to see, touch, and lay whoop-ass on ghosts with barely any trouble ( sometimes), even niftier powers, and actually being alive and able to still enjoy all the stuff you like doing.. what would you choose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T06:50:03-07:00","id":191346,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/184210-choice-become-a-vampire-or-a-geist?p=191157#post191157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent moral dilemmas. But what about this: Okay, so you have been drained dry, the Geist is talking to you and telling these things as it offers you the Bargain. Moral Crossroad Theater aside, what really sounds more appealing; coming back from the dead a slavering corpse that feeds on the life blood of the living and gets the worst case of sunburn when the sun hasn't even risen over the horizon in exchange for possibly immortality and nifty powers.. OR coming back from the dead with a ghostly pseudo buddy, the ability to see, touch, and lay whoop-ass on ghosts with barely any trouble ( sometimes), even niftier powers, and actually being alive and able to still enjoy all the stuff you like doing.. what would you choose?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd choose the Geist any day of the week. Dosen't even have that much to do with being dead and drinking blood (although those are certainly factors). To me, immortality, especially the lifeless immortality of vampires, isn't really something to be desired. I'd much rather have a hand full of good years as a living dude, with a ghostly voice in the back of my head making requests, than I would an eternity of lifelessness.<br /> In my opinion, Vampires are by far the ones who have it the hardest. Prometheans have it harder on a day-to-day basis, but they atleast have the promise of salvation. Vampires dont. They just have an eternity of shit to deal with, and no light at the end of the tunnel. Its just an endless bucket of shit you have pouring over you constantly. Sometimes the shit might not smell that bad, and eventually you might even get used to it. But that dosen't the fact that you're covered in shit, and theres more to come.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T10:38:01-07:00","id":191526,"title":"","content":"^Yeah, that sounds exactly like what the Geist should say. Good stuff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Of, course, WE know that being a vampire is awesome. (Awesome in an RPing sense. Obviously being any WoD splat involves much tragic and dark suffering.)<br /> <br /> Of course, the Geist likely also forgot to mention some of the small print in the bargain, or that it has its own agenda, and if you fail to help it, good luck dealing with plummeting Synergy...<br /> <br /> (Excellent opportunity to play the Geist as a dark and mysterious entity, which may be feared by the rest of the WoD and thus make you powerful too, but brings more trouble to you than you thought when you accepted the bargain...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T16:52:26-07:00","id":191810,"title":"","content":"In <i>Balance of Shadows</i>, we have a Sin-Eater whose wife is a Penanggalan and wants to figure out how to turn her into a Penanggalan too. This is not a big secret...she discovered the girl was a Penanggalan when they started dating (she knew she was undead by looking at her because Sin-Eater). Trying to turn a Sin-Eater into a Penanggalan would not work...she would just come back. So the Penanggalan is trying to find another way. The Sin-Eater is not so crazy about this, but the Penanggalan is worried about what she might become when the Sin-Eater passes away. It's an...interesting dilemma.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T12:35:44-07:00","id":192632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/184210-choice-become-a-vampire-or-a-geist?p=191526#post191526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course, the Geist likely also forgot to mention some of the small print in the bargain, or that it has its own agenda, and if you fail to help it, good luck dealing with plummeting Synergy...</div> </div> </div> </div>That may be so, though the Geist is still very much the passenger up until you get to Synergy 3 or lower when it can take overt command of the body. But until then, even though it has an goal of it's own, the host's priorities typically are the ones that are followed. not to mention that Synergy is probably one of the most forgiving Morality Stats next to Harmony, the danger is much lower than lets say dealing with the frenzied howling of the Beast for Vampires, and the repercussions of losing control of yourself at somewhat slight provocations- dangers the majority of Sin-eaters usually have nothing to worry about. The Bargain is quite preferable to the Embrace, at least with a Geist you are capable of reasoning with it- to a much greater extent than with the Beast at any rate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T14:11:59-07:00","id":193970,"title":"","content":"^I'm not sure what we are arguing about. Sin-Eaters being a better splat than Vampires? Obviously, no. (There are far more Vampire players out there.) Being presented as less tragic in game fiction? Obviously, you do not present a situation like this as an obvious one-sided choice. What the game fiction in general suggests, and much more how you translate what the rules suggest into game fiction, is hugely irrevelant. If you can't present a Geist as a menacing presence when the story asks for it as well, you ain't worth your salt as a GM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T15:44:43-07:00","id":194031,"title":"","content":"I think what is being argued is the objectively better choice, or which is a better choice to the given poster. You can spin it however, and make any changes to make it more appealing, in your game. But in general, the argument is about which is a better choice in general. Certainly, if it were Geist vs. Vampire as better games I'd be making sure it did not get too heated.<br /> <br /> In general, though, one game is presented as a curse, going out of it's way to speak of the hollowness of the condition. The other has a celebratory view of the splat, though it is absolutely not without it's downsides, there is an embracing life theme. So if people are saying Sin-Eater seems more obvious, that is because they are looking at the themes and conditions of the games. They are answering the question, not saying it is a bad question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T16:24:42-07:00","id":194088,"title":"","content":"But arguing which is <i>objectively</i> better is pointless because there is no such thing. SOme players will like vampires more because they feel S-Es are lonelier. Or because they feel they have a bleaker view of the afterlife. Or because they think that constantly having to be exposed to how people died is a pain. Or because they feel that the vampire powers are niftier.<br /> It's fine to post what you <i>subjectively</i> would pick if you were in this situation, but there is no reason to argue that anyone should accept S-Es as objectively better because the rules/fluff sez that they should.<br /> (I mean, even the example with Synergy can be flipped over: vampires are inherently morale creatures while S-Es have no issues with any kind of crime (as their morality is currently written). Which may be a &quot;yay, Iget to do what I want!&quot; thing for some, but &quot;oh fu-, these guys just do what they want without any concern&quot; for another.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T16:57:52-07:00","id":194106,"title":"","content":"You wanted to know what was being discussed. What was being discussed is what you and I addressed.<br /> <br /> People are going to subjectively like one or the other better. More importantly (for a game) their characters are going to subjectively like one or the other better. That's fine. Given that choice, more people would, I think, prefer being a Sin-Eater, for a lot of reasons. That does not mean it is the only answer, or it would have been a bad question (it wasn't) but we are discussing a game where one line uses terms like &quot;Curse&quot; and Requiem&quot; while the other talks about &quot;Second Chances&quot; and &quot;New Beginnings.&quot; That's not a judgment on either line, both lines are awesome and I enjoy both.<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to shut down your question. I'm explaining why some of the comments were as strong for a side. That does not mean there is no room for discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T19:05:24-07:00","id":202544,"title":"","content":"I figure I'd add my (somewhat crude) attempt at a Geist for just such a character concept. <br /> <br /> FATHER BLOOD <br /> Quote: (Vaguely latin gibberish) <br /> Background: It is said by some Geists do not remember their human lives. And Blood does have trouble remembering the day to day living of his mortal self. But the important parts are all too clear. He was a priest, in a small village where no authority besides the church had authority in anything but name since the Romans left. He was a good man(or so his memory says), and gave guidance and aid to his flock. Then She came. She claimed to seek the wisdom of God, but the Leech-Woman only wanted power. With her wicked blood-magics(and great beauty, though he refuses to acknowledge such failings on his part), she twisted his mind and heart, and gave him blood thrice to bind him as her eternal Ghoul. She used him to cover up her indiscretions and find her food, but mostly used her &quot;lover&quot; for her enjoyment. Again and again, she forced him to break every code and stricture he held dear, laughing as he screamed and prayed for mercy. And one day, she pushed too far, and he screamed not in pain, but rage, and used the blood-powered strength she gave him to pin her to the floor of the old wooden church house with a sword(a trophy she took from the corpse of her last &quot;lover&quot; once she tired of him). He set alight the structure, turned, and bit hard upon her neck, giddy with vengeance and Vitae even as his flesh burned black. But he could not stay dead, for she had oft complaint of her fellows, and so long as one of her blighted kin stalked the faithful, he could never stay his undying hatred. And now, centuries later, he has found a proper ally in his fight against the Leaches( &quot;Daeva&quot; they call themselves), a young man drained dry by one in the blasphemous ritual required to create more of their kind. With Blood's aid, he slaughtered the unprepared abomination, and now lives to protect others from his fate. He is young and weak, so he is reluctant to kill, but Blood knows he can bring him around with just a little more time... <br /> Apperance: Blood appears as a corpse wearing the uniform of a catholic priest from the dark ages, torn and filthy in a way that exposes his limbs and torso, covered in puncture wounds like that of a snake bite, each oozing blood at a steady rate. His face, however, is a charred and blackened skull, its teeth sharpened and lengthened into a parody of a serpent's fangs. <br /> Storytelling hints: Father Blood is presented as a theoretical antagonist, though he could easily be a player's Geist. As an antagonist, he is quite willing to drive his partner insane if it means he'll be willing to kill without question, and doesn't care who gets caught in the crossfire. <br /> Threshold: Torn <br /> Virtue: Justice- The Vampires will pay for the lives they've ruined. <br /> Vice: Wrath-And he doesn't care how many innocents have to burn for his vendetta... <br /> Keys: Pyre-Flame(He killed and died by flame), Stigmatica(He was a Ghoul, and has become obsessed with the &quot;Leaches&quot;) <br /> <br /> I don't have a good enough grasp of the mechanics to go on, but I hope I've helped someone out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}